SUMMARY:Another Long One Folks!
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**Meetup Point: 155 Rowntree 
 Mill Rd\, North York\, ON M9L 2K1**\n**Steeles Avenue West and the Humber 
 River\, where it connects with Thackeray Park off Kipling Avenue/Steeles A
 venue**\n\nJoin Honey for a scenic\, full length hike along the Humber Riv
 er through parks\, wooded valley sections\, wetlands\, the Old Mill area a
 nd down to Lake Ontario at Humber Bay Arch Bridge\,\nWe will hike the 20.4
  km point-to-point route from the north to south following the park. It's 
 not a difficult hike but it is long.\n\n**If you are a beginner this might
  not be the hike for you as the pace is steady and the distance is far.**\
 nCome prepared with good walking shoes\, lots of water\, snacks and layers
  as who knows what the weather will be like.\n\nNote: We are like the post
 man. Rain or shine we hike!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/event
 s/317269694/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261103T134214Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T134214Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_317147528@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261107T055712Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T153000
SUMMARY:Hike with James and Gabriel on the Seaton Trail!
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**Meet Up Location: 405 White
 vale Rd. Whitevale\, ON\, L1X 0J9**\n\nJoin James and Gabriel for a modera
 te to challenging hike that includes hills\, wooden and metallic stairs. T
 he path winds tightly along West Duffins Creek through deep cedar forests\
 , lush wetlands\, and open valley meadows.\nSeaton Trail offers a variety 
 of lengths and It's a great all year trail to hike year round.\nWe will hi
 ke 10kms and based on how the group does we will increase the kms\,\nPleas
 e dress appropriately as the weather is changing. Wear solid hiking shoes\
 , bring a lunch and ensure ankles and arms are covered as there are still 
 ticks out there! Lots of water please.\nLots of stretching afterwards!\nNo
 te: Ignore road closure signs for local traffic.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/event
 s/317147528/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261026T162139Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261026T162139Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_316483006@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261107T055712Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T223000
SUMMARY: Practical Philosophy Social!
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\nGet to know your fellow hiker
 s more intimately with a night of Practical Philosophy.\n\nIn partnership 
 with the Practical Philosophy Meetup I thought it would be a fun a social 
 !\n**How does it work?**\nWe select a topic like monogomy vs pologomy and 
 in groups of 6-8 with a moderator (so conservations are respectful)\nten q
 uestions are asked and everyone has a chance to give their take on the sub
 ject.\nGet to know your fellow hikers on a deeper level! You may be surpri
 sed!\n**Opposing views are of course welcome!**\nLocation to be determined
 !
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/event
 s/316483006/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260909T133559Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T133559Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_317270156@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261107T055712Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T163000
SUMMARY:Beaver Valley Loop!
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**Meetup Location: 235082 Gre
 y County Rd 13\, Flesherton**\n**(features roadside parking and Bruce Trai
 l access across the road) [[1](https://www.google.com/searchviewer/10?svid
 =CAwSHRIbCgNwdnESFENnMHZaeTh4TVdkaU5ERXpaemRzGAo)]**\n\n**Rated: Challengi
 ng**\nWe haven't done this one in about two years!\n\nThe Beaver Valley Lo
 op is a premier endurance challenge on the Bruce Trail\, offering a divers
 e journey through one of Ontario's most scenic valleys. This demanding loo
 p links the iconic Eugenia Falls and Hogg's Falls\, taking hikers on a rol
 lercoaster of steep ascents and descents that accumulate over 1\,300 meter
 s of elevation gain. The route traverses a mix of lush forests\, open ski 
 hills with panoramic views\,\n\nDepending on how everyone does we will pla
 y the distance by ear. It is a bit of a trek from Toronto but worth it as 
 it is a great hike. Give yourself plenty of time to get there please as it
  will be a full day.\n\nCome prepared! Hiking poles\, good hiking shoes\, 
 lots of water and snacks!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/event
 s/317270156/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261103T142718Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T142718Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_317270342@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261107T055712Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T153000
SUMMARY:Hike with the Dancing King (aka Robin)- Hockley Valley
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**MeetUp Location: Hockley Va
 lley PP/Bruce Trail Parking just off Hwy 7**\n\nFor those of you who join 
 our parties\, you know Robin is the the Dancing King! He also leads a wick
 ed hike. Join Robin on the 14.2 km trail through the Hockley Valley.\nThis
  loop-to-loop trail brings you over rivers\, wee waterfalls and bridges\, 
 winds and dines you through diverse forests filled with incredible varieti
 es of fungus - you might even wonder if you just landed in British Columbi
 a. And just when you get yourself used to piney forest goodness\, you'll p
 op out into hilly meadows filled with wildflowers. Those 12 km deliver so 
 many different landscapes\, smells\, sounds\, an abandoned jalopy and pure
  joy. This hike is going to get your heart pumping and your body sweaty\, 
 but the trail is a mere minutes drive from Adamo Estate winery. So after t
 raversing for 12km\, a glass of dry crisp rose is the icing on the cake wh
 ile sitting in Muskoka chairs overlooking the vineyards.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/event
 s/317270342/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261103T144704Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T144704Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: These Boots Are Made for Hiking
UID:event_317270510@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261107T055712Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261206T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261206T153000
SUMMARY:Join Mo on a Hike to Rattlesnake Point...hissss
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**Meetup Point: Meet up point
 : Northern end of Walkers line.**\n**Address: 7365 Walkers Line\, Milton\,
  ON L9T 2Y1**\n**GPS Coordinates: 43.467015\, -79.929050 (or 43°28'01.3"N
  79°55'44.6"W)**\n**Parking is free**\nHiking with Mo is always a treat! 
 You will be guaranteed a history lesson or a bad joke!\nThis hike hits the
  sweet spot for intermediate hikers\, blending the rugged terrain of the *
 *Niagara Escarpment** with dramatic cliffside views without requiring an e
 xhausting all-day commitment.\nHike Overview\nBegin your trek on a wide\, 
 forested path that gradually transitions into the the escarpment terrain 
 —packed with exposed cedar roots\, limestone steps\, and uneven rock for
 mations that will keep your feet engaged.\nThe highlight of the route is t
 he stretch along the cliff edges\, From this vantage point\, you will stan
 d high above the Lowville Valley\, looking down on the canopy and watching
  turkey vultures ride the thermal updrafts right at eye level. Keep an eye
  out for the ancient\, twisted cliff-edge cedars\, some of which have surv
 ived here for over 800 years.\nThis is a great hike at this time of year!\
 nPlease ensure you have proper footwear\, lots of water and snacks!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/event
 s/317270510/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261103T150424Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T150424Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
